\ A recognized #map keeps its vectorized chain only while no method has been registered on
\ the arithmetic it matched. Registering one part-way through a drain retires the chain and
\ hands every element that has not been yielded yet to the quotation. Isolated from the
\ other packed tests because these registrations mutate global dispatch state.

use "testing" ;
use "math/packed" ;

"method registered mid-drain" test-section

{ 1.0 2.0 3.0 } >packed:f64 [ 2.0 * ] #map
dup #next 2.0 "first element still vectorized" assert=
*: method{ float float } [ drop drop 999.0 ] ;
#collect { 999.0 999.0 } "remaining elements honor the mid-drain method" assert=

"the bail is element-exact across a chunk" test-section

\ Eight elements span more than one SIMD chunk, so the first #next leaves the rest of its
\ chunk computed but unyielded. Those are rewound and recomputed, not handed over.
8 3.0 packed-fill:f64 [ 1.0 + ] #map
dup #next 4.0 "first element still vectorized" assert=
+: method{ float float } [ drop drop 5.0 ] ;
#collect { 5.0 5.0 5.0 5.0 5.0 5.0 5.0 } "no element of the computed chunk survives the bail" assert=

"a chain recognized after the registration is never built" test-section

\ The creation-time guard refuses the same method the drain-time guard bails on, so a #map
\ built now takes the scalar path from its first element.
{ 1.0 2.0 } >packed:f64 [ 4.0 * ] #map #collect { 999.0 999.0 } "recognition refused up front" assert=
